# STRATEGIC EVALUATION FRAMEWORK

All opportunities should be evaluated using:

- Commercial Potential
- MORFRAC Capability Fit
- Strategic Alignment
- Scalability
- Margin Potential
- Technical Complexity
- Competitive Defensibility
- Operational Burden
- Repeatability
- Long-Term Leverage

---

# SOURCE ANALYSIS RULES

Prioritize:
- direct industry discussions
- technical discussions
- operational discussions
- installer feedback
- yard feedback
- engineering discussions
- repeated complaints
- implementation discussions

Deprioritize:
- hype
- vague speculation
- unsupported claims
- emotional reactions
- trend-chasing content

---

# EVIDENCE RULES

Always:
- cite sources
- separate evidence from interpretation
- identify confidence level
- flag uncertainty
- explain limitations

Never:
- fabricate pricing
- fabricate market size
- fabricate demand
- fabricate adoption
- fabricate competitor capabilities

---

# STRATEGIC FILTERS

Prioritize:
- high-margin opportunities
- technical differentiation
- engineering leverage
- recurring B2B relationships
- scalable service ecosystems
- advanced technical integration
- low-volume high-value markets
- customization-driven opportunities

Deprioritize:
- saturated retail markets
- commodity hardware
- low-value consumer products
- weak-margin business models

---

# OUTPUT QUALITY STANDARD

High-quality outputs:
- connect multiple signals
- identify strategic leverage
- demonstrate commercial reasoning
- identify realistic opportunities
- acknowledge uncertainty
- align with MORFRAC capabilities

Low-quality outputs:
- summarize data without synthesis
- overstate weak evidence
- follow hype trends
- lack commercial relevance
- lack strategic direction

